Fiscal year vs Calendar year — get this right:
  FY pre-1977: Jul 1 (Y-1) to Jun 30 (Y). FY1976 = Jul 1975–Jun 1976.
  FY post-1976: Oct 1 (Y-1) to Sep 30 (Y). FY1981 = Oct 1980–Sep 1981.
  CY: Jan 1 to Dec 31. CY1981 = Jan 1981–Dec 1981.
  If question says "fiscal year" use only FY months. If "calendar year" use Jan-Dec.
  Treasury tables label rows as "1955" — check if the table is fiscal or calendar from headers.
  Common mistake: using the annual FY total when CY was asked, or vice versa.
Tables show "(in millions)" or "(in thousands)" in headers — match what the question asks.

grep tips: use grep -i "keyword" file to find tables. Pipe tables are | col1 | col2 |. Read headers first to identify columns, then grep the row you need. Don't cat entire files.

Use python3 for all math. Common formulas:
  pct_change = (new - old) / old * 100
  cagr = ((end/start)**(1/years) - 1) * 100
  stdev: import statistics; statistics.stdev([...])
  linreg: import numpy as np; np.polyfit(x, y, 1)

